# Assurance policy: gdc / simulation.  NEVER use in production.
#
# Grants the highest tier to a wallet whose client CLAIMS to use the soft
# plugin, so a test environment without hardware can exercise issuers that
# demand high key storage / user authentication. Both rules depend on
# client-claimed evidence on purpose; the linter warns about them.
#
# The client must send security_properties.plugin = "soft".
#
# With lower_by_claims_* = true (the default) the result is min(claimed,
# granted), so the granted tier only shows up when the client also claims the
# target level. Set lower_by_claims_key_storage / _user_authentication to
# false to let these rules be the sole authority.

# id: gdc-soft-ks-high
(assure-ks (tier (* set basic enhanced-basic moderate high))(evidence (verified)(claimed (plugin soft))))

# id: gdc-soft-ua-high
(assure-ua (tier (* set basic enhanced-basic moderate high))(evidence (verified)(claimed (plugin soft))))
